  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In the kitchen, Fedya reads a bizarre statistic about falling coconuts while Senya brags that a coconut could never knock him out, leading to a reckless bet right as Chef Barinov speaks with the inspector.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "От падения кокосов гибнут люди.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Что это за полный бред?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "На меня кокос уже падал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Ну я же совсем живой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Ты не выдержишь удар кокосом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я не выдержу такой удар?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Давай тогда с тобой замажем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Так я получу эту звезду?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надеюсь, у нас будет отлично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Кокосы никогда не предупреждают заранее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Можешь бросить в меня кокос.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Может завтра, а может сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "От падения кокосов гибнут люди.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'People die from falling coconuts.' Notice how Russian expresses 'from' and 'people' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Что это за полный бред?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What kind of total nonsense is this?' Notice how Russian expresses 'what' and 'nonsense' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "На меня кокос уже падал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A coconut has already fallen on me.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'on' before landing on 'to fall'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Ну я же совсем живой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, I am completely alive.' Senya anchors the line on 'come on', while 'alive' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Ты не выдержишь удар кокосом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You will not withstand a blow from a coconut.' Notice how Russian expresses 'you' and 'with a coconut' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я не выдержу такой удар?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will not withstand such a blow?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'I' before landing on 'blow'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Давай тогда с тобой замажем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let us make a bet then.' In Russian, the idea of 'come on' flows naturally into 'let us bet' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Так я получу эту звезду?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So will I get this star?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'so' and finishing on 'star'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надеюсь, у нас будет отлично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I hope everything will be great for us.' Notice how Russian expresses 'hope' and 'perfectly' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Кокосы никогда не предупреждают заранее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Coconuts never warn you in advance.' The grammar packs 'coconuts' and 'in advance' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Можешь бросить в меня кокос.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You can throw a coconut at me.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'can' and 'to abandon' in a few short words. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Может завтра, а может сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maybe tomorrow, or maybe right now.' Fedya anchors the line on 'maybe', while 'now' completes the thought. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "От падения кокосов гибнут люди.",
